<section class="pactsol-charges">
  <div class="site-container pactsol-charges__grid">

    <div class="pactsol-charges__intro">

      <p class="pactsol-charges__label">
        How PACTSOL Charges
      </p>

      <h2>
        Clear commercial terms before you commit.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Submitting a sourcing requirement to PACTSOL is free. If a
        requirement is suitable for further sourcing support, the applicable
        commercial arrangement will depend on the nature of the requirement,
        the supplier relationship, and the transaction structure.
      </p>

    </div>

    <div class="pactsol-charges__details">

      <article>
        <span>01</span>

        <div>
          <h3>
            No charge to submit a requirement
          </h3>

          <p>
            Businesses may share a sourcing requirement with PACTSOL for
            initial review without paying a submission fee.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>02</span>

        <div>
          <h3>
            Buyer sourcing or service fee
          </h3>

          <p>
            Where a sourcing or service fee is payable directly by the
            customer, the applicable fee and scope will be communicated
            before the customer commits to the relevant service or
            transaction.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>03</span>

        <div>
          <h3>
            Supplier-side commercial commission
          </h3>

          <p>
            In some transactions, PACTSOL may receive an agreed commercial
            commission from a supplier for business introduced or sourcing
            activity coordinated by PACTSOL.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span>04</span>

        <div>
          <h3>
            No fixed public percentage
          </h3>

          <p>
            PACTSOL does not presently apply a single fixed public commission
            or sourcing-fee percentage across all products or transactions.
            Commercial arrangements may vary according to the requirement,
            product category, sourcing effort, and applicable supplier terms.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>




